Step 1. Understanding the Mission

• The mission is to collect required resources from one or more storage locations and deliver them to a specified destination.
• The process is divided into two phases:
 – Collection Phase: The robot navigates to storage(s), sends a message with the resource specification, and waits for retrieval.
 – Delivery Phase: The robot navigates to the destination and makes as many runs as needed.
• Battery management is critical:
 – In the collection phase, if the battery drops below 10%, the robot must return to the recharging station and reassign the mission.
 – In the delivery phase, if the battery drops below 30%, the robot must return the resource to a checkpoint and reassign the remaining task.
 – If the fallback (returning to checkpoint) fails, an alert must be triggered and a report sent to the sector manager.
• Additionally, if multiple storages are involved, robots may be assigned in parallel to reduce mission time.

